# Per-package USE flags — Orange Pi 4 LTS (Rockchip RK3399, arm64) light
# desktop. Mirrors specs-frite/portage/package.use/frite
# almost verbatim — these are cross-compile-toolchain gaps, not SoC-specific
# ones, and this platform shares the SAME aarch64 cross toolchain + hardened
# profile + lean-LXDE package set as Frite/RPi5.

# gentoo-sources: install the source symlink so the kernel build can find it.
sys-kernel/gentoo-sources symlink

# parted needs device-mapper for the installer's partitioning helpers.
sys-block/parted device-mapper

# NetworkManager: keep wifi USE (the onboard brcmfmac radio is described and
# enabled in the mainline device tree this image boots) but the radio is
# rfkill-blocked + module-blacklisted by default (harden_radios in the builder)
# — see specs-orangepi4-lts/README.md.
net-misc/networkmanager wifi

# Lean desktop USE trims:
#   xterm: no toolbar bloat.
x11-terms/xterm -toolbar

# freetype needs harfbuzz to satisfy pango, which openbox, GTK+, elogind, dbus,
# and dracut all depend on transitively. Without this the entire desktop stack
# fails to emerge (autounmask stops backtracking and per-package fallback
# repeats the same failure for every package in that dep chain).
media-libs/freetype harfbuzz

# ngtcp2 needs gnutls to satisfy net-fs/samba pulled in by net-fs/cifs-utils[acl].
net-libs/ngtcp2 gnutls

# libdom needs xml to satisfy www-client/netsurf[svgtiny,svg].
net-libs/libdom xml

# gtk+ rsvg USE disabled: librsvg is a Rust crate; cross-compiling it to aarch64
# requires the aarch64-unknown-linux-gnu Rust stdlib target on the host, which
# is absent from the system dev-lang/rust installation (only x86_64 and i686
# targets are installed). SVG cursor/icon rendering is non-essential on a
# minimal LXDE desktop. adwaita-icon-theme is listed in profile/package.provided
# (below) to satisfy gtk+'s RDEPEND without actually building the package
# (which also needs librsvg).
x11-libs/gtk+ -rsvg

# libfm automount disabled: with +automount, libfm unconditionally requires
# gnome-base/gvfs. gvfs has +gcr by default which requires app-crypt/gcr:4=,
# which requires gui-libs/gtk-4, which fails to cross-compile. gvfs[keyring]
# also pulls in app-crypt/libsecret, which in turn pulls gnome-keyring -> gcr-3
# -> virtual/secret-service. Disabling automount removes the ENTIRE gvfs dep and
# its cascading GTK4/libsecret chain. pcmanfm still functions for local
# filesystem browsing; USB auto-mounting can be added post-first-boot via
# native emerge.
x11-libs/libfm -automount

# networkmanager modemmanager USE disabled: +modemmanager pulls modemmanager ->
# libqmi[qrtr] -> net-libs/libqrtr-glib -> dev-libs/gobject-introspection ->
# glib with introspection enabled. Our global -introspection breaks this chain.
# Cellular modems are absent from these SBC targets; disabling modemmanager has
# no functional impact.
net-misc/networkmanager -modemmanager

# pinentry gtk USE disabled: +gtk causes pinentry to require app-crypt/gcr:4[gtk],
# which in turn requires gui-libs/gtk-4 (fails cross-configure). The ncurses/
# curses pinentry backend (kept via the global gtk USE not applying to
# pinentry's own -gtk) is sufficient for passphrase prompts on this lean-desktop
# SBC.
app-crypt/pinentry -gtk
